                  P
                  =
                  0.001
                
              
              ) and earlier age of onset (
              
                
                  P
                  =
                  0.043
                
              
              ) predicted the conversion of CIS to McDonald MS. Gender (
              
                
                  P
                  =
                  0.5
                
              
              ) and initial clinical presentation (optic pathway (
              
                
                  P
                  =
                  0.4
                
              
              ), supratentorial (
              
                
                  P
                  =
                  0.91
                
              
              ), brain stem/ cerebellum (
              
                
                  P
                  =
                  0.97
                
              
              ), and spinal (
              
                
                  P
                  =
                  0.76
                
              
              )) were not statistically significant.
              Conclusion
              . Age of onset and MRI parameters can be used as predictors of CIS conversion to McDonald MS. Application of the 2010 revised McDonald criteria  allows an earlier MS diagnosis.},
