              ; and for the second, the best results were obtained for the 6th year of progression, also within two years: AUC=
              
                
                  \$\$0.89{\textbackslash}pm 0.03\$\$
                  
                    
                      0.89
                      ±
                      0.03
                    
                  
                
              
              , sensitivity=
              
                
                  \$\$0.84{\textbackslash}pm 0.11\$\$
                  
                    
                      0.84
                      ±
                      0.11
                    
                  
                
              
              , and specificity=
              
                
                  \$\$0.81{\textbackslash}pm 0.05\$\$
                  
                    
                      0.81
                      ±
                      0.05
                    
                  
                
              
              . The Expanded Disability Status Scale value, the majority of functional systems, affected functions during relapses, and age at onset were described as the most predictive features. These results demonstrate the possibility of predicting Multiple Sclerosis progression by using machine learning, which may help to understand this disease’s dynamics and thus, advise physicians on medication intake.},
